### Version 1.0.1 (unreleased)

- Refactored the SDK around one canonical C++ implementation and pybind11
  bindings under the existing `fourier_aurora_client` import.
- Added an explicit restartable singleton lifecycle, selective endpoints,
  SDK-owned data types, robot-independent diagnostic clients, standalone GR3
  recipes, and deterministic Debian and wheel verification.
- Replaced numeric lease Source IDs with required, human-readable Source Names.
- Reduced protected-command Lease Information to the authority-issued Lease ID
  and per-stream sequence, and adopted the pod message namespace.
- Added the `aurora-client-NNNN` convenience identity for the packaged CLI while
  keeping Source Name explicit for direct C++ and Python callers.
- Standardized robot-facing CLI writes as `state set`, `motion set`, and
  `control-group set`.
- Replaced the generic FSM `SetInt` service payload with attributed,
  machine-readable state-switch requests and added explicit forced admission
  through the C++, Python, and CLI clients.
- Added separate standard-GIL CPython 3.10 through 3.13 Linux wheels.
- Established the initial C++ ABI at `SOVERSION 1` and requires
  `fourier-dds-msgs 0.2.0-1`.
